  "goodToKnow": "Die Fahrerlaubnis is the official term for a driving licence, the legal right to drive; der Führerschein is the card proving it, and the word people use in daily life. After serious offences such as drink driving, a court can withdraw it (Entzug der Fahrerlaubnis), and getting it back may require the MPU, a medical-psychological assessment nicknamed Idiotentest. Teenagers can drive accompanied from 17 (begleitetes Fahren). Plural: die Fahrerlaubnisse."
